==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|Ты}} {{q|religious}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|тꙑ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*ty}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*túh₂}}. Cognate with {{cog|cu|тꙑ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-ты.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|ru|pronoun|cat2=personal pronouns}}

# {{lb|ru|familiar}} second-person singular, nominative case: [[you]], [[thou]]
#* {{quote-book|ru|author= w:ru:Лазарь Лагин<t:{{w|Lazar Lagin}}>|year= 1972|origyear= 1955, 1938|title= lw:ru:Старик Хоттабыч|chapter= Беспокойный вечер|page= 42
|newversion= English translation based on|translator2= Faina Solasko|year2= 1960
|title2= The Old Genie Hottabych|chapter2= A Troubled Evening|page2= 51|pageurl2= https://archive.org/details/lazar-lagin-the-old-genie-hottabych-flph-1950/page/51/mode/2up
|text=— А ну, подойди́-ка побли́же, недосто́йная прислу́жница! Мне не нра́вится, как '''ты''' отве́тила на приказа́ние моего́ ю́ного дру́га и повели́теля.
|translation= “Come near, unworthy servant! I don’t like how '''thou''' hast answered to the orders of my young friend and master.”}}

====Usage notes====
The personal pronoun {{lang|ru|ты}} is comparable to French {{m|fr|tu}}, German {{m|de|du}}, and is used only with family and intimate friends. In classical literature, it is used by superiors to their inferiors, but that usage is no longer tolerated (with the exception of the way adults speak to children, while the children are expected to use вы). For most occasions, the formal {{m|ru|вы}} should be used instead. For more information, see [[Appendix:Russian pronouns]].

